    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0429" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg419"/>

                <head>Her Majesty’s Treasury to Laird Brothers.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#top">
                        <table cols="3">
                            <row>
                                <cell role="num">209</cell>
                                <cell role="brace" rows="2">}</cell>
                                <cell rows="2">20/1</cell>
                            </row>
                            <row>
                                <cell role="num">464</cell>
                            </row>
                        </table></seg></opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Chambers,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: In reply to your letter of the 9th
                    instant, and previous letters, I am commanded, by the lords commissioners of her
                    Majesty’s treasury, to acquaint you that their lordships will provide, in the
                    manner they may consider requisite, against the risks from fire and other
                    damages to the iron-clad vessels El Tousson and El Monnassir, while they remain
                    in possession of her Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>I am, gentlemen, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. A. HAMILTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laird,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Birkenhead Iron Works, Birkenhead,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
